te TD overturned by replay was incorrect decision, MAC says","description":"A Kent State touchdown catch should not have been overturned by replay to incomplete at the end of Tuesday's 17-12 loss to Eastern Michigan, the Mid-American Conference said Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-25T23:05:40.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50597875/kent-state-td-overturned-replay-was-incorrect-mac-says","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 College Football Playoff National Championship odds","description":"Odds and futures to win the 2027 College Football Playoff National Championship.","published":"2026-11-25T19:44:57.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/47664633/2027-college-football-playoff-national-championship-odds-futures","type":"Story","byline":"Doug Greenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Chris Creighton out as coach at Eastern Michigan after 13 seasons","description":"Chris Creighton is out as head coach at Eastern Michigan after 13 seasons with the school.","published":"2026-11-25T19:05:05.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50595706/creighton-coach-eastern-michigan-13-seasons","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Judge denies SEC's request for TRO against LSU in Dec. 3 vote","description":"A federal judge denied the SEC's request for a temporary restraining order to keep LSU from interfering with a Dec. 3 vote of presidents and chancellors on whether to remove the school from the conference.","published":"2026-11-25T20:02:54.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-sports/story/_/id/50595702/judge-denies-sec-request-tro-lsu-dec-3-vote","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 13 Game Day Kickoff: Nothing compares to the outright hatred of a rival","description":"What to expect in Rivalry Week, from top games and players to teams on upset alert.","published":"2026-11-25T19:44:59.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/gamedaykickoff112526/week-13-top-games-upsets-preview","type":"Story","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Oklahoma State extends Morris with new 6-year deal","description":"Oklahoma State and head coach Eric Morris have agreed to a new six-year deal that will extend his contract through the 2032 season, sources told ESPN's Pete Thamel on Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-25T17:00:56.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50594432/sources-oklahoma-state-extends-morris-new-six-year-deal","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Where is 'College GameDay'? 2026 schedule, locations, recaps","description":"What is the \"College GameDay\" schedule? Find out more about where the program will be each week of the 2026 college football season.","published":"2026-11-25T15:16:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49783645/where-college-gameday-2026-schedule-locations-recaps","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4881031/jamari-sharpe","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamari_Sharpe"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jamari Sharpe","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamari_Sharpe","description":"American football player (born 2003)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:24Z","intro":"Jamari Sharpe (born September 22, 2003) is an American college football defensive back for the Indiana Hoosiers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Sharpe was born September 22, 2003, in Miami, Florida. He attended Miami Northwestern Senior High School, where he played wide receiver on the school's football team before changing to cornerback in his senior year. Sharpe and Northwestern won a state championship in 2019. He also competed in track and field, placing sixth in the 100-meter dash and second on the 4 × 100 team at state finals."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"A three-star college football recruit, Sharpe committed to play for the Indiana Hoosiers beginning in 2022 as part of the school's highest-ranked recruiting class in program history. He redshirted the 2022 season after appearing in three games. In 2023, he played in all 12 games with nine starts, recording 22 tackles, three pass breakups, and one interception. He appeared in nine games with three starts in 2024, including a start in Indiana's 2024–25 College Football Playoff game against the Notre Dame Fighting Irish, recording 13 tackles, six pass breakups, one fumble recovery, and 0.5 sacks on the season.\nSharpe was named the likely starter for the 2025 season by head coach Curt Cignetti during preseason training camp. In a win against the Oregon Ducks, as Sharpe left the field with an injury, the broadcast showed Cignetti appearing to tell Sharpe to \"toughen up\"; Sharpe returned to the game one play later. Sharpe caught the game-sealing interception of a Carson Beck pass against the Miami Hurricanes in the 2026 College Football Playoff National Championship, which won Indiana their first national championship in program history."}]}}